1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,235
In this lesson, you'll build
your first workflow from scratch.

2
00:00:04,235 --> 00:00:08,873
When someone fills in your contact form,
Kyntlo will text them straight away,

3
00:00:08,873 --> 00:00:12,246
tell your team, and send a
follow-up email the next day.

4
00:00:12,246 --> 00:00:14,414
Then we'll test it and switch it on.

5
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:16,229
Why start here?

6
00:00:16,229 --> 00:00:17,448
Because speed wins.

7
00:00:17,448 --> 00:00:21,811
People who fill in a form are often
contacting other businesses too.

8
00:00:21,811 --> 00:00:25,019
An instant, friendly reply,
even an automated one,

9
00:00:25,019 --> 00:00:28,804
keeps you first in line while
your team gets ready to call.

10
00:00:29,662 --> 00:00:33,289
Go to Automation, then Workflows,
and click Create Workflow.

11
00:00:33,289 --> 00:00:36,493
You can start from a recipe,
which we'll cover later,

12
00:00:36,493 --> 00:00:41,449
but this time choose Start from Scratch,
so you see how every piece fits together.

13
00:00:42,298 --> 00:00:44,040
First, give it a clear name.

14
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:49,204
Click the title at the top and type something
you'll recognise in six months' time,

15
00:00:49,204 --> 00:00:51,257
like Contact Form, Instant Reply.

16
00:00:52,109 --> 00:00:53,138
Now the trigger.

17
00:00:53,138 --> 00:00:55,905
Click Add New Trigger,
and search for form.

18
00:00:55,905 --> 00:00:57,321
Choose Form Submitted.

19
00:00:57,321 --> 00:01:01,696
Then add a filter, so only the
Contact Us form starts this workflow,

20
00:01:01,696 --> 00:01:03,176
and click Save Trigger.

21
00:01:06,417 --> 00:01:10,647
Next, click the plus button under
the trigger to add an action.

22
00:01:10,647 --> 00:01:14,004
Every action lives in this
panel, grouped by type.

23
00:01:14,004 --> 00:01:16,489
Under Communication, choose Send SMS.

24
00:01:17,342 --> 00:01:18,554
Write your message.

25
00:01:18,554 --> 00:01:23,020
To greet each person by name, click
Custom Values and pick First Name.

26
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:28,061
Kyntlo swaps that placeholder for each
contact's real first name when it sends.

27
00:01:28,061 --> 00:01:31,187
Keep it short and friendly,
then save the action.

28
00:01:32,037 --> 00:01:33,566
Now let your team know.

29
00:01:33,566 --> 00:01:35,626
Add Send Internal Notification.

30
00:01:35,626 --> 00:01:40,212
By default it alerts the user assigned
to the contact, inside Kyntlo,

31
00:01:40,212 --> 00:01:43,336
so the right person can
call them back quickly.

32
00:01:44,188 --> 00:01:48,517
If they haven't heard from you by
tomorrow, a follow-up email helps.

33
00:01:48,517 --> 00:01:51,508
Add a Wait action, set
it to one day, and save.

34
00:01:51,508 --> 00:01:55,392
Then add Send Email underneath,
with a friendly subject line.

35
00:02:01,102 --> 00:02:03,810
Before going live, check the Settings tab.

36
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:08,904
Stop on response is on, so anyone who
replies stops getting automated messages,

37
00:02:08,904 --> 00:02:10,967
and a real person can take over.

38
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:16,190
You can also set a time window, so texts
never go out in the middle of the night.

39
00:02:17,043 --> 00:02:21,016
Back in the builder, click Test
Workflow, and choose a contact.

40
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:24,485
Test on yourself, because
the messages are really sent.

41
00:02:24,485 --> 00:02:27,891
Run the test, and you'll see
each step as it executes.

42
00:02:27,891 --> 00:02:31,108
It stops at the wait,
exactly as a real lead would.

43
00:02:32,773 --> 00:02:35,308
Everything works, so let's switch it on.

44
00:02:35,308 --> 00:02:38,730
Flip the toggle from Draft
to Publish, and click Save.

45
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:43,610
From now on, every Contact Us submission
gets an instant reply, day or night.

46
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:45,507
Here's a pro tip.

47
00:02:45,507 --> 00:02:48,401
Read your messages as if
you were the customer.

48
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:51,973
Would this text make sense on
its own, at any time of day?

49
00:02:51,973 --> 00:02:53,574
Does it say who it's from?

50
00:02:53,574 --> 00:02:54,744
If not, rewrite it.

51
00:02:54,744 --> 00:02:57,946
Workflows are only as good
as the words inside them.

52
00:02:58,799 --> 00:03:02,929
Congratulations, you've built and
published your first workflow!

53
00:03:02,929 --> 00:03:07,705
Next, we'll make workflows smarter
with If/Else branches, waits and goals.

54
00:03:07,705 --> 00:03:09,448
See you in the next lesson.
